new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI, TAKAAKI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUJIWARA TETSUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HIGASHIYAMA KAZUTOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NABATAME TOSHIHIDE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI TAKAAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUJIWARA, TETSUO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIGASHIYAMA, KAZUTOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NABATAME, TOSHIHIDE</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI, TAKAAKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A semiconductor device including a dielectric element which has an element structure of high aspect ratio resulting from large-scale integration and an excellent step coverage and a method for manufacturing the same are disclosed.  A lower electrode (46) and an upper electrode (48) both made of homogeneous Ru thin film and having 100 % step coverage are formed on both sides of an electric body (47) on underlying substrates (44, 45) having a roughness of an aspect ratio of 3, thereby manufacturing a large-scale integrated dielectric element in the temperature range from 180 DEG  to 250  DEG C by an MOCVD method using cyclopentadienyl complex.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne un dispositif semi-conducteur comprenant un élément diélectrique qui présente une structure à rapport longueur-diamètre élevé autorisant une intégration à grande échelle et une excellente couverture en gradins. Une électrode inférieure (46) et une électrode supérieure (48), qui sont toutes deux faites d'un mince film homogène de Ru et qui ont un pouvoir couvrant sur les gradins de 100 %, sont formées de part et d'autre d'un élément électrique (47) sur les substrats sous-jacents (44, 45), avec un rapport longueur-diamètre de 3. L'invention concerne également la fabrication d'un élément diélectriques intégré à grande échelle sous des températures comprises entre 180 et 250  DEG C, selon un procédé de dépôt chimique métal-oxyde en phase vapeur au moyen d'un complexe cyclopentaldiényl.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>